; e129_sock_connect_in_refused.chiral — E129 conformance: the AF_INET connect-ERROR path.
;
; sock-connect-in runs parse-quad (pure) -> pack-sa-in (pure, big-endian port)
; -> nb-sock-connect-in (the fused socket(2,1,0)+connect crossing) against
; 127.0.0.1:1 — a closed port, so connect() returns -ECONNREFUSED. The fused
; TAL body closes the fd (else leak) and assembles (conn-err "") via ti-cona.
; Exit 42 = the conn-err arm reached: socket + connect + errno decode all ran
; natively on-target, and the ConnR sum was built and cased. HERMETIC (no peer,
; no listener, no network — port 1 is closed on this host).
;
; The conn-r SUCCESS arm is compiled but UNREACHED here (chirality has no listener
; yet — sock-listen/sock-accept are deferred). It MUST be present: QTT requires
; the linear Sock bound by conn-r to be consumed (sock-close, E107), so a
; missing arm fails the checker, not just coverage.
;
; LINEAR DISCIPLINE: every arm of the ConnR case consumes every live cap. The
; conn-err arm carries only a Str (no cap to thread — the fd is already closed
; inside the crossing). The conn-r arm owes the Sock and discharges it with
; sock-close. This is the same shape as e127_sock_connect_err.chiral.
;
; DISCRIMINATING: the OLD B1 (pre-E129) has no crossing-wraps row for
; nb-sock-connect-in and no inet.chiral surface, so it cannot compile this at all.
(import "prelude/prelude")
(import "ports/ports")
(import "protocol/inet")

(def compile-main (=> I64 I64)
  (lam (n)
    (case (sock-connect-in "127.0.0.1" 1)
      ((conn-err m) 42)
      ((conn-r s)
        (case (sock-close s)
          (unit 0))))))
